Pins what jellyfin's builder takes from the day of the build, for the toolchain images.

* crosstool-NG at 185f3483 (1.28.0-23), the version its ct-ng-config names (CT_VERSION
  "1.28.0.23_185f348"). The builder cloned its main, which no longer has the config's gcc 15.2.0
  and binutils 2.46.0: those were then fetched with no digest to check and none of their bundled
  patches, since ct-ng build reads the .config as written.
* GNU packages from ftp.gnu.org, GNU's own server: CT_Mirrors no longer offers ftpmirror.gnu.org,
  which redirects to a mirror picked at random, and one served an ncurses-6.5.tar.gz whose
  sha512 was not the release's (2026-10-30; the digest check refused it).
* ubuntu:resolute by digest, the image of 2026-10-29.
* Implib.so at a3e167cf, its head since 2026-08-01, instead of its head on the day.

diff --git a/builder/images/base-linux64/Dockerfile b/builder/images/base-linux64/Dockerfile
index 0af1d29e..72ea22ea 100644
--- a/builder/images/base-linux64/Dockerfile
+++ b/builder/images/base-linux64/Dockerfile
@@ -3,6 +3,8 @@ FROM $GH_REPO/base:latest
 
 RUN --mount=src=ct-ng-config,dst=/.config \
     git clone --filter=blob:none https://github.com/crosstool-ng/crosstool-ng.git /ct-ng && cd /ct-ng && \
+    git checkout 185f3483e0e5028357b131fb97c4331551a70a1e && \
+    sed -i '/ftpmirror\.gnu\.org/d' scripts/functions && ! grep -q ftpmirror scripts/functions && \
     rm -rf packages/linux/*/chksum && \
     ./bootstrap && \
     ./configure --enable-local && \
@@ -38,7 +40,8 @@ ADD toolchain.cmake /toolchain.cmake
 ADD cross.meson /cross.meson
 
 ADD gen-implib.sh /usr/bin/gen-implib
-RUN git clone --filter=blob:none --depth=1 https://github.com/yugr/Implib.so /opt/implib
+RUN git clone --filter=blob:none https://github.com/yugr/Implib.so /opt/implib && \
+    git -C /opt/implib checkout a3e167cf978a5b8a38ec0f710d8c4331e8dcdd9a
 
 ENV FFBUILD_TOOLCHAIN=x86_64-ffbuild-linux-gnu
 ENV PATH="/opt/ct-ng/bin:${PATH}" \
